Weber, based on the 2012 novel of the same name by John Green.

13
01:11:13,043 --> 01:11:19,043
The film stars Shailene Woodley and Ansel Elgort, with Laura Dern, Sam
Trammell, Nat Wolff, and Willem Dafoe in supporting roles.

14
01:16:41,739 --> 01:16:47,739
The story centers on a sixteen-year-old cancer patient, played by Woodley, forced by her parents to attend a support
group, where she meets and subsequently falls in love with another cancer patient, played by Elgort.

15
01:22:10,434 --> 01:22:16,434
Development began in January 2012 when Fox 2000 Pictures optioned the film
adaptation rights to adapt the novel into a feature film.

16
01:27:39,130 --> 01:27:45,130
Principal photography began on August 26, 2013, in Pittsburgh, with a few additional
days in Amsterdam, The Netherlands, before concluding on October 16.

17
01:33:07,826 --> 01:33:13,826
Pittsburgh doubled for all of the scenes set in Indianapolis, Indiana, the
novel's setting, as well as for some interior scenes set in Amsterdam.

18
01:38:36,521 --> 01:38:42,521
The Fault in Our Stars had its premiere at the Seattle International Film Festival on May 16, 2014, and was released in the United States on June 6 by 20th
Century Fox to favorable reviews, with praise being given to Woodley's and Elgort's performances and chemistry together, as well as the screenplay.

19
01:44:05,217 --> 01:44:11,217
The film opened at number one at the box office during its opening weekend and grossed
$307.2 million worldwide against a production budget of $12 million.

